Falsifies `calendar::verification::the_calendar_algorithms_are_mutual_inverses`.

The defect: `civil_from_days` drops the `- doe / 146_096` term from its year-of-era estimate, the
correction for the 400-year exception to the century rule. The last day of every 400-year era then
decodes to the wrong year and `days_from_civil` maps it back to a different day.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_eq!(days_from_civil(y, m, d), days)`.

diff --git a/crates/calendar/src/lib.rs b/crates/calendar/src/lib.rs
index 332ce0020..94a32d635 100644
--- a/crates/calendar/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/calendar/src/lib.rs
@@ -232,3 +232,3 @@ const fn civil_from_days(days: i64) -> (i32, u8, u8) {
     // back the century non-leaps, /146096 removes the 400-year exception to that exception.
-    let yoe = (doe - doe / 1460 + doe / 36_524 - doe / 146_096) / 365; // [0, 399]
+    let yoe = (doe - doe / 1460 + doe / 36_524) / 365; // [0, 399]
     let y = yoe + era * 400;
